cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SAICA-Bench, its results or the SAICA-KG data, please cite it as below."
title: SAICA-Bench
abstract: >-
  SAICA-Bench measures whether supervision tools and language models catch
  the typical failures of AI coding agents (fabrication, test manipulation,
  security vulnerabilities, logic errors, incomplete execution, scope creep,
  obsolescence, supply-chain attacks, dependency blindness). Every reviewer
  sees the same labelled samples and is scored J = TPR - FPR, with the cost
  per 1,000 reviews. The repository also holds SAICA-KG, a knowledge graph of
  failure modes, supervision tools, papers, incidents and external taxonomies.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vasyl
    family-names: Rakivnenko
    affiliation: Stanford University
url: "https://saica.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vasylrakivnenko/SAICA"
